-- title:
--   Flat classes in ad ρ̄ and in its cyclotomic dual twist
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field of characteristic $p$ with $p$ an odd prime, and fix a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\bar\rho$ and $\bar\rho'$ be residual Galois representations over $k$, each consisting of a $k$-vector space $V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (as $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$) to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field. Suppose given a $k$-linear isomorphism $\eta$ from $\bar\rho'.V$ onto the $k$-dual of $\bar\rho.V$ satisfying, for every $g$ and every $w$, $\eta(\bar\rho'.\rho(g)\,w) = \chi(g)\cdot\big(\eta(w)\circ \bar\rho.\rho(g^{-1})\big)$, where $\chi(g)\in k$ is the image of the value at $g$ of the mod $p$ cyclotomic character `cycloChar p` (obtained from the modular cyclotomic character on $p$-th roots of unity) under the canonical map $\mathbb{Z}/p \to k$; thus $\bar\rho'$ is the dual of $\bar\rho$ twisted by the mod $p$ cyclotomic character. The conclusion is that the type of $k$-linear equivalences between $\bar\rho.\mathrm{localFlatClassesAd}\,p$ and $\bar\rho'.\mathrm{localFlatClassesAd}\,p$ is nonempty. Here, for a residual representation, $\mathrm{localFlatClassesAd}\,p$ is the $k$-submodule of the first group cohomology of the restriction along `primeLocalToGlobal (pPrime p)` of the conjugation representation $\mathrm{ad}$ on $\mathrm{End}_k V$, spanned by the classes of those $1$-cocycles $c$ for which there exist a commutative ring $H$ carrying a cocommutative $\mathbb{Z}_p$-Hopf algebra structure, finite and flat as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module, and a bijection $e$ from the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra maps $H \to \mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\,p$ (with their convolution group law) onto $V \times V$ carrying that law to addition and intertwining the local Galois action on points with the action `dualLiftModuleActAd p c` on $V \times V$.
--
--   This is the self-duality of the flat (finite flat model) local condition at $p$ under Cartier duality: the transpose isomorphism $\mathrm{ad}\,\bar\rho \cong \mathrm{ad}(\bar\rho^\vee(1))$ carries flat classes to flat classes, because the Cartier dual of a finite flat model of the dual-lift module of a cocycle is a finite flat model for the twisted dual cocycle. It is used in the computation of local deformation invariants at $p$, and is cited in the production of unipotent models together with the comparison of flat classes under base change.
